<title>UK: Mexico to issue 300 mln stg five-yr bond - BZW/SBCW.</title>
<headline>Mexico to issue 300 mln stg five-yr bond - BZW/SBCW.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico has awarded BZW and SBC Warburg the mandate to lead manage a sterling bond which was most likely to be a 300 million stg five-year offering, BZW said on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>&quot;The deal will be around 300 million stg,&quot; a BZW syndicate manager said.</p>
<p>No further details were made available.</p>
<p>Mexico was last in the international bond market on April 17 with a 500 billion lire 20-year issue via Deutsche Morgan Grenfell.</p>
<p>-- Dan Lalor, London newsroom +44 171 542 8863</p>
